==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|orv|вьрвь}} + {{af|ru|-ка}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*vьrvь}} (deverbal of {{m|sla-pro|*verti}}), from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*wer-|t=to tie, string; rope}} which is ultimately cognate with {{m|ine-pro|*wer-|t=to turn, bend}} whence the two meanings of the verb. Compare {{cog|be|вяроўка}}, {{cog|uk|верве́чка}}, {{cog|cu|връвь}}. Non-Slavic cognates include {{cog|lt|virvė}}, {{cog|lv|virve}}, {{cog|ltg|vērve||rope, cord, line}}, {{cog|grc|ἐρύω|t=I drag, pull}} and {{cog|sa|वरत्रा}}.

